packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:3:Available agent types and the tools they have access to:
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:6:When using the Task tool, you must specify a subagent_type parameter to select which agent type to use.
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:8:When to use the Task tool:
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:9:- When you are instructed to execute custom slash commands. Use the Task tool with the slash command invocation as the entire prompt. The slash command can take arguments. For example: Task(description="Check the file", prompt="/check-file path/to/file.py")
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:11:When NOT to use the Task tool:
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:12:- If you want to read a specific file path, use the Read or Glob tool instead of the Task tool, to find the match more quickly
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:13:- If you are searching for a specific class definition like "class Foo", use the Glob tool instead, to find the match more quickly
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:14:- If you are searching for code within a specific file or set of 2-3 files, use the Read tool instead of the Task tool, to find the match more quickly
packages/opencode/src/tool/task.txt:19:1. Launch multiple agents concurrently whenever possible, to maximize performance; to do that, use a single message with multiple tool uses
