     5	
     6	OpenCode integrates with your Language Server Protocol (LSP) to help the LLM interact with your codebase. It uses diagnostics to provide feedback to the LLM.
     7	
     8	---
     9	
    10	## Built-in
    11	
    12	OpenCode comes with several built-in LSP servers for popular languages:
    13	
    14	| LSP Server         | Extensions                                                          | Requirements                                                 |
    15	| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
    16	| astro              | .astro                                                              | Auto-installs for Astro projects                             |
    17	| bash               | .sh, .bash, .zsh, .ksh                                              | Auto-installs bash-language-server                           |
    18	| clangd             | .c, .cpp, .cc, .cxx, .c++, .h, .hpp, .hh, .hxx, .h++                | Auto-installs for C/C++ projects                             |
    19	| csharp             | .cs                                                                 | `.NET SDK` installed                                         |
    20	| clojure-lsp        | .clj, .cljs, .cljc, .edn                                            | `clojure-lsp` command available                              |
    21	| dart               | .dart                                                               | `dart` command available                                     |
    22	| deno               | .ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs                                          | `deno` command available (auto-detects deno.json/deno.jsonc) |
    23	| elixir-ls          | .ex, .exs                                                           | `elixir` command available                                   |
    24	| eslint             | .ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .mts, .cts, .vue                  | `eslint` dependency in project                               |
    25	| fsharp             | .fs, .fsi, .fsx, .fsscript                                          | `.NET SDK` installed                                         |
    26	| gleam              | .gleam                                                              | `gleam` command available                                    |
    27	| gopls              | .go                                                                 | `go` command available                                       |
    28	| hls                | .hs, .lhs                                                           | `haskell-language-server-wrapper` command available          |
    29	| jdtls              | .java                                                               | `Java SDK (version 21+)` installed                           |
    30	| julials            | .jl                                                                 | `julia` and `LanguageServer.jl` installed                    |
    31	| kotlin-ls          | .kt, .kts                                                           | Auto-installs for Kotlin projects                            |
    32	| lua-ls             | .lua                                                                | Auto-installs for Lua projects                               |
    33	| nixd               | .nix                                                                | `nixd` command available                                     |
    34	| ocaml-lsp          | .ml, .mli                                                           | `ocamllsp` command available                                 |
    35	| oxlint             | .ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .mts, .cts, .vue, .astro, .svelte | `oxlint` dependency in project                               |
    36	| php intelephense   | .php                                                                | Auto-installs for PHP projects                               |
    37	| prisma             | .prisma                                                             | `prisma` command available                                   |
    38	| pyright            | .py, .pyi                                                           | `pyright` dependency installed                               |
    39	| ruby-lsp (rubocop) | .rb, .rake, .gemspec, .ru                                           | `ruby` and `gem` commands available                          |
    40	| rust               | .rs                                                                 | `rust-analyzer` command available                            |
    41	| sourcekit-lsp      | .swift, .objc, .objcpp                                              | `swift` installed (`xcode` on macOS)                         |
    42	| svelte             | .svelte                                                             | Auto-installs for Svelte projects                            |
    43	| terraform          | .tf, .tfvars                                                        | Auto-installs from GitHub releases                           |
    44	| tinymist           | .typ, .typc                                                         | Auto-installs from GitHub releases                           |
    45	| typescript         | .ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .mts, .cts                        | `typescript` dependency in project                           |
    46	| vue                | .vue                                                                | Auto-installs for Vue projects                               |
    47	| yaml-ls            | .yaml, .yml                                                         | Auto-installs Red Hat yaml-language-server                   |
    48	| zls                | .zig, .zon                                                          | `zig` command available                                      |
    49	
    50	LSP servers are automatically enabled when one of the above file extensions are detected and the requirements are met.
    51	
    52	:::note
    53	You can disable automatic LSP server downloads by setting the `OPENCODE_DISABLE_LSP_DOWNLOAD` environment variable to `true`.
    54	:::
    55	
    56	---
    57	
    58	## How It Works
    59	
    60	When opencode opens a file, it:
    61	
    62	1. Checks the file extension against all enabled LSP servers.
    63	2. Starts the appropriate LSP server if not already running.
    64	
